  {
    "title": "You don’t get to define me",
    "file": "../audio/You don’t get to define me.mp3",
    "description": "A song about empowerment and reclaiming ownership of my life, reminding others that my path is mine alone. In the end, no one gets to define who you are, because your life belongs to you.",
    "album": "Hope",
    "releaseDate": "2026-06-15",
    "lyrics": "you dont get to define me\n\nYou studied me like broken language\nLike I was something to explain\nSpoke in cold and borrowed answers\nNever touched an ounce of pain\n\nEvery mirror held a stranger\nEvery birthday felt like loss\nLearned to hide inside the silence\nLearned exactly what it costs\n\nYou only saw the smoke\nNever where the fire began\n\nI am not your war to fight\nNot your fear to weaponize\nNot a target for your anger\nJust because I chose my life\n\nI bled to become this person\nThrough every scar you left behind\nSay whatever helps you sleep\nYou don’t get to define me\n\nyou dont get to define me\n\nYou disguise contempt as concern\nWrap your cruelty up as care\nNever seeing what your words do\nNever feeling what lives there\n\nHow many break behind closed doorways\nTrying hard to just survive?\nHow many learn to hate their breathing\nJust to keep your world alive?\n\nYour black-and-white world never fit\nA heart that had to fight to live\n\nI am not your war to fight\nNot your fear to weaponize\nNot a target for your anger\nJust because I chose my life\n\nI bled to become this person\nThrough every scar you left behind\nSay whatever helps you sleep\nYou don’t get to define me\n\nyou dont get to define me\n\nThere were nights I begged for silence\nThought disappearing meant relief\nBut the voice beneath the wreckage\nStill refused to leave me\n\nI AM NOT YOUR WAR TO FIGHT\nNOT YOUR FEAR TO WEAPONIZE\nI SURVIVED YOUR EXPECTATIONS\nAND I CAME OUT ALIVE\n\nI bled to become this person\nI won’t disappear this time\nSay whatever helps you sleep\nYou don’t get to define me\n\nyou dont get to define me"
  }
